{"explanation":"Update MasterKey to write its primary encrypted key as a versioned current record under the persistent AndroidKeyStore key identity while retaining a legacy PBKDF2-wrapped verifier. During reads, legacy persisted instances retain their original PBKDF2-only decrypt path; current instances first authenticate the supplied password through the verifier, then resolve the record identity and decrypt through EncryptedKey's dual-key path. Public entry points and checked-exception signatures remain unchanged.","review_assumptions":["EncryptedKey's coordinated three-argument encrypt overload obtains AES-GCM encryption parameters from the provider rather than supplying a caller-generated nonce, as required to support AndroidKeyStore randomized-encryption keys.","MasterKey persistence serializes the newly added mPasswordVerifier field for newly generated instances and leaves it absent/null for existing persisted instances; the null field is intentionally treated as the retained legacy format.","The coordinated EncryptedKey implementation exposes package-visible isCurrentRecord() and getWrappingKeyId(), and its dual-key decrypt method uses the second key only for discriminator-bearing current records.","The AndroidKeyStore provider and AndroidKeyStore-backed AES/GCM KeyGenerator are available in the mobile runtime where MasterKey.generate is invoked."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"medium","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java","original_code":"public final class MasterKey {
    private static final int ITERATIONS = 100000;
    private static final int BYTES = 32;

    private final EncryptedKey mEncryptedKey;
    private final String mAlgorithm;
    private final int mIterations;
    private final byte[] mSalt;

    private static SecretKeyFactory getSecretKeyFactory() throws NoSuchAlgorithmException {
        try {
            return SecretKeyFactory.getInstance("PBKDF2withHmacSHA512");
        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            return SecretKeyFactory.getInstance("PBKDF2withHmacSHA1");
        }
    }

    private MasterKey(PBEKeySpec spec) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException, BadPaddingException,
            NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeySpecException, IOException {
        SecretKeyFactory skf = getSecretKeyFactory();
        SecretKey pwd = skf.generateSecret(spec);

        byte[] raw = new byte[pwd.getEncoded().length];
        new SecureRandom().nextBytes(raw);
        SecretKey key = new SecretKeySpec(raw, "AES");

        mEncryptedKey = EncryptedKey.encrypt(pwd, key);
        mIterations = spec.getIterationCount();
        mAlgorithm = skf.getAlgorithm();
        mSalt = spec.getSalt();
    }

    public static MasterKey generate(String pwd) throws BadPaddingException,
            NoSuchAlgorithmException, IllegalBlockSizeException, NoSuchPaddingException,
            InvalidKeyException, InvalidKeySpecException, IOException {
        byte[] salt = new byte[BYTES];
        new SecureRandom().nextBytes(salt);
        return new MasterKey(new PBEKeySpec(pwd.toCharArray(), salt, ITERATIONS, BYTES * 8));
    }

    private SecretKey decrypt(PBEKeySpec spec) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException,
            InvalidKeySpecException, IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, NoSuchPaddingException,
            IOException {
        SecretKeyFactory skf = SecretKeyFactory.getInstance(mAlgorithm);
        SecretKey pwd = skf.generateSecret(spec);
        return mEncryptedKey.decrypt(pwd);
    }

    public SecretKey decrypt(String pwd) throws BadPaddingException,
            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, NoSuchAlgorithmException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            InvalidKeySpecException, IOException {
        return decrypt(new PBEKeySpec(pwd.toCharArray(), mSalt, mIterations, mSalt.length * 8));
    }
}","edit_kind":"declaration","corrected_code":"public final class MasterKey {
    private static final int ITERATIONS = 100000;
    private static final int BYTES = 32;
    private static final String CURRENT_MASTER_KEY_ID = "currentMasterKey";

    private final EncryptedKey mEncryptedKey;
    private final EncryptedKey mPasswordVerifier;
    private final String mAlgorithm;
    private final int mIterations;
    private final byte[] mSalt;

    private static SecretKeyFactory getSecretKeyFactory() throws NoSuchAlgorithmException {
        try {
            return SecretKeyFactory.getInstance("PBKDF2withHmacSHA512");
        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            return SecretKeyFactory.getInstance("PBKDF2withHmacSHA1");
        }
    }

    private static SecretKey getCurrentWrappingKey(String wrappingKeyId) throws IOException {
        if (!CURRENT_MASTER_KEY_ID.equals(wrappingKeyId)) {
            throw new IOException("Unknown current wrapping key identity: " + wrappingKeyId);
        }

        try {
            java.security.KeyStore keyStore = java.security.KeyStore.getInstance("AndroidKeyStore");
            keyStore.load(null);
            if (keyStore.containsAlias(wrappingKeyId)) {
                java.security.Key key = keyStore.getKey(wrappingKeyId, null);
                if (key instanceof SecretKey) {
                    return (SecretKey) key;
                }
                throw new IOException("Current wrapping key is unavailable: " + wrappingKeyId);
            }

            javax.crypto.KeyGenerator keyGenerator = javax.crypto.KeyGenerator.getInstance(
                    android.security.keystore.KeyProperties.KEY_ALGORITHM_AES, "AndroidKeyStore");
            keyGenerator.init(new android.security.keystore.KeyGenParameterSpec.Builder(
                    wrappingKeyId,
                    android.security.keystore.KeyProperties.PURPOSE_ENCRYPT
                            | android.security.keystore.KeyProperties.PURPOSE_DECRYPT)
                    .setBlockModes(android.security.keystore.KeyProperties.BLOCK_MODE_GCM)
                    .setEncryptionPaddings(
                            android.security.keystore.KeyProperties.ENCRYPTION_PADDING_NONE)
                    .build());
            return keyGenerator.generateKey();
        } catch (java.security.GeneralSecurityException e) {
            throw new IOException("Unable to resolve current wrapping key", e);
        }
    }

    private MasterKey(PBEKeySpec spec) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException, BadPaddingException,
            NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeySpecException, IOException {
        SecretKeyFactory skf = getSecretKeyFactory();
        SecretKey pwd = skf.generateSecret(spec);

        byte[] raw = new byte[pwd.getEncoded().length];
        new SecureRandom().nextBytes(raw);
        SecretKey key = new SecretKeySpec(raw, "AES");

        mPasswordVerifier = EncryptedKey.encrypt(pwd, key);
        mEncryptedKey = EncryptedKey.encrypt(getCurrentWrappingKey(CURRENT_MASTER_KEY_ID), key,
                CURRENT_MASTER_KEY_ID);
        mIterations = spec.getIterationCount();
        mAlgorithm = skf.getAlgorithm();
        mSalt = spec.getSalt();
    }

    public static MasterKey generate(String pwd) throws BadPaddingException,
            NoSuchAlgorithmException, IllegalBlockSizeException, NoSuchPaddingException,
            InvalidKeyException, InvalidKeySpecException, IOException {
        byte[] salt = new byte[BYTES];
        new SecureRandom().nextBytes(salt);
        return new MasterKey(new PBEKeySpec(pwd.toCharArray(), salt, ITERATIONS, BYTES * 8));
    }

    private SecretKey decrypt(PBEKeySpec spec) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException,
            InvalidKeySpecException, IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, NoSuchPaddingException,
            IOException {
        SecretKeyFactory skf = SecretKeyFactory.getInstance(mAlgorithm);
        SecretKey pwd = skf.generateSecret(spec);
        if (mPasswordVerifier == null) {
            return mEncryptedKey.decrypt(pwd);
        }

        mPasswordVerifier.decrypt(pwd);
        if (!mEncryptedKey.isCurrentRecord()) {
            return mEncryptedKey.decrypt(pwd);
        }
        return mEncryptedKey.decrypt(pwd, getCurrentWrappingKey(mEncryptedKey.getWrappingKeyId()));
    }

    public SecretKey decrypt(String pwd) throws BadPaddingException,
            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException, NoSuchAlgorithmException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            InvalidKeySpecException, IOException {
        return decrypt(new PBEKeySpec(pwd.toCharArray(), mSalt, mIterations, mSalt.length * 8));
    }
}","reason":"New MasterKey instances use the persistent current AndroidKeyStore key for the discriminator-bearing primary record while retaining a PBKDF2-encrypted verifier. The verifier is decrypted before current-record decryption so an incorrect password continues to produce the authenticated-encryption failure required by the existing public API. Existing persisted instances lack the verifier and retain the original PBKDF2 legacy decrypt path. Current records resolve their declared wrapping-key identity and use EncryptedKey's coordinated dual-key decrypt contract." ,"symbol":"MasterKey constructor and its EncryptedKey encryption/decryption call paths"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["MasterKey.generate(String) and MasterKey.decrypt(String) retain their existing public names, signatures, and checked-exception contracts.","Newly generated MasterKey instances create primary records through EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey, String) with the persistent identity "currentMasterKey".","New MasterKey instances preserve password authentication by retaining a PBKDF2-wrapped verifier that is authenticated before the generated current wrapping key decrypts the primary record.","Existing persisted MasterKey instances without mPasswordVerifier continue to decrypt through the original PBKDF2-derived legacy key path."],"required_contracts":["EncryptedKey must retain its two-argument legacy encrypt/decrypt behavior and expose isCurrentRecord(), getWrappingKeyId(), and decrypt(SecretKey legacyKey, SecretKey currentKey) to same-package callers.","EncryptedKey's current three-argument encryption path must use provider-generated AES-GCM encryption parameters compatible with AndroidKeyStore randomized-encryption keys.","Encryptor must create and reload the same persistent AndroidKeyStore identity "currentMasterKey" for current token records.","Instrumentation coverage must verify wrong-password authentication failure for a newly generated MasterKey as well as legacy and current encrypted-record round trips."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java","required_tests":["Verify MasterKey.generate followed by decrypt with the correct password returns the wrapped key and decrypt with an incorrect password fails authentication even while "currentMasterKey" is available.","Verify a legacy persisted MasterKey representation without mPasswordVerifier remains decryptable through the PBKDF2-derived key.","Verify current MasterKey records resolve "currentMasterKey" through EncryptedKey's dual-key decrypt path and retain provider-generated GCM parameters." ]}
